Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 has no wheels for lxml/numpy/pandas/matplotlib; this build excludes netedit/GUI entirely (CLAUDE.md gotcha 682), so none of the four are ever imported]

Upstream's build-system.requires lists lxml, numpy, pandas and matplotlib
purely to enable netedit's optional runtime tool-detection ("all
dependencies below (except for scikit) are just to enable the tool
detection in netedit", per upstream's own comment). This workflow builds
with ENABLE_FOX=OFF/ENABLE_PYTHON_BINDINGS=OFF and packages only
tools/build_config/sumo (no netedit/GUI), which never imports any of the
four.

None of them has a riscv64 wheel on PyPI, so PEP 517 build isolation was
source-building the entire stack before scikit-build-core even starts,
and it failed two hours in: numpy/pandas/matplotlib/contourpy built fine,
but matplotlib's own dependency Pillow does not, since this workflow's
CIBW_BEFORE_ALL_LINUX deliberately skips upstream's
install_dependencies.sh (which installs libjpeg-turbo-devel only for the
GUI/FOX leg we don't build):

  RequiredDependencyException: jpeg
  The headers or library files could not be found for jpeg, a required
  dependency when compiling Pillow from source.

Installing libjpeg-turbo-devel would just make a multi-hour from-source
build of a stack we never use succeed before throwing the result away.
Dropping the four down to scikit-build-core alone removes dead weight for
this wheel configuration and fixes the build.

diff --git a/build_config/pyproject/eclipse-sumo.toml b/build_config/pyproject/eclipse-sumo.toml
index 3693fdf5b5..37169fb000 100644
--- a/build_config/pyproject/eclipse-sumo.toml
+++ b/build_config/pyproject/eclipse-sumo.toml
@@ -1,11 +1,12 @@
 [build-system]
-# all dependencies below (except for scikit) are just to enable the tool detection in netedit
-requires = [ "scikit-build-core>=0.10",
-    "lxml",
-    "numpy<2.3",
-    "pandas<2.3",
-    "matplotlib"
-]
+# Upstream's lxml/numpy/pandas/matplotlib entries below only enable netedit's
+# optional runtime tool-detection; this wheel packages tools/build_config/sumo
+# only (no netedit/GUI - see build-eclipse-sumo.yml) and never imports them, so
+# they are dropped here rather than built from source: riscv64 has no
+# prebuilt wheels for any of them, and matplotlib's own build pulls in
+# Pillow, which then fails to compile without libjpeg headers we do not
+# install (CLAUDE.md gotcha 682).
+requires = ["scikit-build-core>=0.10"]
 build-backend = "scikit_build_core.build"

 [project]
